#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192568 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192858 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a891eaf9-6a4c-5e87-8aa0-95920347bd4d" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Product as a Repeated Addition"}] :question/id #uuid "56936482-95f9-54ff-b006-cd79247947ba" :question/math-academy-id "e-13618" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd41e0c4d98c28e41c8e91743c70bbcac3e0b88071d1075e1cd518d2410843fa.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above. Write down this multiplication as a repeated addition of fraction models." :question/worked-solution "In the model, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{red}4}{5}\n$$\n\nmultiplied by ${\\color{blue}3}$. This means that we need to make $\\color{blue}3$ copies of the given fraction model.\n\n![](images/2a/2ab193d9bb045165bcfffadae012523f33297548eacbdfd6b3514c791d7fac58.png)\n\nSo, the missing picture is:\n\n![](images/59/59f5625dce754f49724d16b00e839ec34e473601df4702db51f3973f14fd4c10.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192569 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0abaf0f6-4018-54b2-a118-f420a3e0705c" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number Using Repeated Addition"}] :question/id #uuid "6a8062c4-e4e5-5045-8b33-7f0afaf76d72" :question/math-academy-id "e-13624" :question/problem "![](images/15/1553e601de2b1664996bb27d49cb09d3baacc72772f9846b45dc45dc9114ff53.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\dfrac{5}{6} \\times 3$." :question/worked-solution "Since we need to multiply\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{6}\n$$\n\nby $\\color{blue}3$, we repeat the fraction model $\\color{blue}3$ times, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b9/b9443ceedbda3d541b0fc4d69489eead83dc8550710c7b6b3f1f9ed90d1dc97b.png)\n\nThere are\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}5} \\times {\\color{blue}3} = 15\n$$\n\nshaded pieces in total. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{6} \\times 3 = \\dfrac{15}{6}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192570 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192860 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78c0c75e-8a40-5064-a62a-954d8b85c3c1" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number by Repeating the Shaded Parts"}] :question/id #uuid "3c170236-340b-5446-960f-a20b6937c23c" :question/math-academy-id "e-13628" :question/problem "![](images/a7/a7e53c31ac53ee142500771bf19af2995c02ecb6fef9aa37e73402e63fa7d518.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the multiplication problem above?" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{7}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{6}{7}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/a7/a7b6a481c90b7372d0b78f7029b3fe8ae9c9c98f484459e1b7697308e3e2ebce.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $3$ shaded pieces, and the shape on the right has $6$ shaded pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of ${\\color{blue}2}$. (That is, the number of shaded pieces has been multiplied by ${\\color{blue}2}$.)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{7} \\times {\\color{blue}2} = \\dfrac{6}{7}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is ${\\color{blue}2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0abaf0f6-4018-54b2-a118-f420a3e0705c" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number Using Repeated Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98866497-3825-5973-b47c-06e21b63be0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192112} {:answer/id #uuid "9a071f3e-4f32-5ce8-afff-c32f84e35a9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192113} {:answer/id #uuid "d01de287-3da4-5469-98f2-0d8e6f4a2df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192114} {:answer/id #uuid "e5081161-4b08-5267-9301-fdec6f15675f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192115} {:answer/id #uuid "fe688ae7-cf91-59af-8d11-49b92456cba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192116}] :answer-field/id #uuid "45997166-5c22-5ec4-b916-247b51dea41d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192111}] :question/id #uuid "c53f7f8f-8ef7-5317-a65a-a39660f0f70b" :question/math-academy-id "q-59976" :question/problem "![](images/a0/a013d4e6e0a7aced6662208bb2c1e42c46de68c0f4f8aef360585aa7ea805334.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $2 \\cdot \\frac{2}{5}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192860 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78c0c75e-8a40-5064-a62a-954d8b85c3c1" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number by Repeating the Shaded Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91e7af7e-45d4-5c68-a7ea-9db8935af859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{8} \\cdot 2 = \\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192136} {:answer/id #uuid "a078fb96-9d4d-5f0d-aad0-cff18c6cae6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{8} \\cdot 2 = \\frac{6}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192137} {:answer/id #uuid "c057ba0e-e211-5d01-84aa-28a04db1df17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8} \\cdot 2 = \\frac{6}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192138} {:answer/id #uuid "10806d7d-1ccf-55d5-9bd7-7628889e60fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{6} \\cdot 4 = \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192139} {:answer/id #uuid "6b283ff6-f2a1-55a1-b214-edf220316fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8} \\cdot 3 = \\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192140}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3520462c-4bd7-5c5e-8157-9e5b6a52a420" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192135}] :question/id #uuid "75df0560-ffa9-56b9-8620-1e3152afc6ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-60195" :question/problem "![](images/1d/1ddc7cb84abc3e8a3fa7cea8e2d43d8cbee6e62e3ea02b99d024581d8b869282.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?"}]}
